sentences.text:
This Court has considered the following facts while exercising discretion in favour of the applicant :-
R/CR.MA/2069/2023 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 (i) the applicant is in jail since 24.04.2021;
(ii) the investigation is over and the charge-sheet is filed;
(iii) the complainant has turned hostile during trial;
(iv) today learned advocate Mr.Jigar Patel for original complainant has tendered an affidavit dated 03.02.2023 of original complainant wherein it is stated that they have decided to bury the grievances and deponent has no objection if the applicant is enlarged on bail as the parties have amicably settled the dispute;
(v) no past antecedent is attributed to the present applicant.
6.

Hence, present application is allowed and the applicant is ordered to be released on regular bail in connection with C.R. No.11196009210138 of 2020 registered with Jawaharnagar Police Station,
District Vadodara on executing personal bond of Rs.10,000/- (Rupees Ten thousand only) with one surety of the like amount to the R/CR.MA/2069/2023 ORDER DATED: 21/04/2023 satisfaction of the learned Trial Court and subject to the conditions that he shall;
[a] not take undue advantage of liberty or misuse liberty;
[b] not act in a manner injuries to the interest of the prosecution;
[c] surrender passport, if any, to the lower court within a week;
Arjun @ Mehul Vijaybhai Parmar vs State Of Gujarat on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/64024317/
2 [d] not leave India without prior permission of the Sessions Judge concerned;
[e] furnish latest address of residence to the Investigating Officer and also to the Court at the time of execution of the bond and shall not change the residence without prior permission of the trial Court;
[f] mark his presence before the concerned police station in the first week of every month till the trial is over;
7.

